.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "October 2023" "Simple Shell" "User  Commands"
.SH NAME
simple_shell \- simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simple_shell
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simple_shell
is a simple UNIX command interpreter that allows users to execute commands in an interactive or non-interactive mode. It mimics the behavior of the standard shell, providing a basic interface for command execution.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Display help information about the shell and its usage.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Display the version of the shell.

.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
When run without any input redirection, the shell operates in interactive mode, displaying a prompt and waiting for user input.

.SH NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
When input is provided through standard input (e.g., using a pipe), the shell operates in non-interactive mode, executing commands as they are received.

.SH EXAMPLES
To run the shell in interactive mode:
.B ./hsh
.PP
To run a command in non-interactive mode:
.B echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.PP
To display help information:
.B ./hsh -h
.PP
To check the version:
.B ./hsh -v

